1
00:00:01,270 --> 00:00:02,400
Hello, everybody.

2
00:00:02,410 --> 00:00:06,970
My name is Lilly and today we'll talk about articles.

3
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:17,470
So articles are such small words a and the, they are so small that some people decide to ignore them.

4
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,240
Well, that's not right.

5
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:23,560
They may be small, but they are very important.

6
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:24,810
Well.

7
00:00:24,810 --> 00:00:29,670
And in this lesson, you will learn everything you need to know about articles.

8
00:00:30,030 --> 00:00:30,930
Let's start.

9
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:41,670
Okay, so in English there are only two types of articles, article a or an and article the.

10
00:00:42,330 --> 00:00:49,020
So a is called an indefinite article and the is called a definite article.

11
00:00:49,920 --> 00:00:54,480
Now articles are used in front of nouns.

12
00:00:57,530 --> 00:00:58,850
The code.

13
00:01:00,770 --> 00:01:02,060
A developer.

14
00:01:04,739 --> 00:01:09,200
Now the important task or a big project.

15
00:01:09,210 --> 00:01:20,670
So this article the refers to task, but in between we have the word describing it important.

16
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:21,740
It's okay.

17
00:01:21,750 --> 00:01:27,270
It can come between an article and the noun.

18
00:01:27,270 --> 00:01:29,850
So the important task.

19
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,680
A big project.

20
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:33,120
What else?

21
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:38,040
We don't use articles with names.

22
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:40,230
We don't say a Lilly.

23
00:01:40,440 --> 00:01:43,110
We don't say the Bill Gates.

24
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:50,070
And we also don't use articles with geographical names.

25
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:55,140
Well, there are some exceptions to that, but we will talk about them a bit later.

26
00:02:00,790 --> 00:02:12,680
And now let's start let's start with the indefinite article a or an. So a is used only in singular.

27
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:13,780
What does it mean?

28
00:02:14,050 --> 00:02:20,710
Well, it means that we can only say a company

29
00:02:20,980 --> 00:02:21,860
Right.

30
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:26,590
We can't say a companies or a money.

31
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:32,920
We use a only with one thing, right

32
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:38,630
If that's hard to remember, just imagine that and means one.

33
00:02:38,630 --> 00:02:41,190
You wouldn't say one companies.

34
00:02:41,630 --> 00:02:44,630
And that's why you shouldn't say a companies.

35
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:48,040
Why cannot we say a money?

36
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:53,890
Well, if you remember, and this was mentioned in our previous course.

37
00:02:54,190 --> 00:02:57,290
Money is uncountable in English.

38
00:02:57,310 --> 00:03:03,070
So with the nouns we can't count like money or time.

39
00:03:03,190 --> 00:03:04,990
We wouldn't use article a.

40
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:06,660
Okay.

41
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,730
What else?

42
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:13,130
You've probably noticed that sometimes we say an, why do we say

43
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:16,340
an instead of a. They are totally the same.

44
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:19,130
Yes, their usage is the same.

45
00:03:19,790 --> 00:03:28,760
But sometimes we say an. Well, that would be before the words that start with those sounds:

46
00:03:29,720 --> 00:03:31,980
a, e, i, o, u.

47
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,070
So they are called vowels.

48
00:03:34,100 --> 00:03:45,650
Well, a e i o u, if you if your word start with one of those letters, usually you would say an. An archive,

49
00:03:45,740 --> 00:03:48,320
an error, an option.

50
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:57,470
Well, this is really convenient because try saying a archive, that's hard, right. 

51
00:03:57,470 --> 00:04:04,130
So it's much easier to say and an archive, an error, an option.

52
00:04:04,910 --> 00:04:13,190
But I want you to be careful here with the letter you. With this latter, letter u.

53
00:04:14,690 --> 00:04:17,959
Well usually we will say an umbrella.

54
00:04:17,959 --> 00:04:23,510
So when the word starts with u, we will say an, an umbrella.

55
00:04:24,420 --> 00:04:33,780
But we will say a user, a utility program, a university and a usb-c port.

56
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,030
Why's that?

57
00:04:36,510 --> 00:04:41,700
Because in the first case, an umbrella you sounds like

58
00:04:41,730 --> 00:04:44,850
"ah", that's vowel, right.

59
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:50,200
And in the second case, a user, we hear u.

60
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:53,850
So technically, the first sound is "j" here.

61
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:54,840
Right.

62
00:04:54,840 --> 00:04:56,100
It's not a vowel.

63
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,510
It's not here.

64
00:04:57,990 --> 00:05:00,210
So pay attention to that little thing.

65
00:05:00,450 --> 00:05:05,430
And also, one more tricky thing would be.

66
00:05:06,240 --> 00:05:07,210
Just a second.

67
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:08,250
Here we go.

68
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:10,260
And hour.

69
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:16,040
And an HR manager. So words starting with h,

70
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:18,650
please pay attention to those as well,

71
00:05:19,220 --> 00:05:30,680
because, well, we have h here, seems like we have to say a, but h is silent.

72
00:05:30,680 --> 00:05:32,330
We don't pronounce it.

73
00:05:32,330 --> 00:05:43,970
That's why the next sound is o. An hour. Well here and HR manager, right

74
00:05:43,970 --> 00:05:46,100
An HR manager.

75
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:52,340
Well, when we say h, h, the first sound is "e".

76
00:05:52,340 --> 00:05:54,020
So like is the name of this letter -

77
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:59,570
h. The first sound is "e", that's why an HR manager.

78
00:05:59,570 --> 00:06:03,260
So just remember an hour, an HR manager.

79
00:06:08,720 --> 00:06:09,350
All right.

80
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:17,390
And now let's talk when we use article a right, when do we have to use article a and not article the.

81
00:06:17,930 --> 00:06:20,120
So here is an example.

82
00:06:20,570 --> 00:06:23,150
I've just got a message from our team lead.

83
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:27,770
I've just got a message from our team lead. 

84
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:34,030
We use article a when we mention something for the first time.

85
00:06:35,020 --> 00:06:41,710
So we just saw that message and we say, Oh, I've just got a message from our team lead.

86
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:44,270
I don't know what the message is about.

87
00:06:44,290 --> 00:06:46,360
I mentioned it for the first time.

88
00:06:46,390 --> 00:06:49,000
Article a. The second one.

89
00:06:49,360 --> 00:06:54,790
CAPTCHA is a program used to verify that a human, not a computer, is entering data.

90
00:06:55,960 --> 00:07:01,630
So we use article a when we explain what something is.

91
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:07,190
We are explaining, we're given a definition like in a dictionary.

92
00:07:07,250 --> 00:07:08,360
What is CAPTCHA?

93
00:07:08,390 --> 00:07:10,940
CAPTCHA is a program.

94
00:07:11,150 --> 00:07:11,660
Right.

95
00:07:11,660 --> 00:07:13,610
We explain what it is.

96
00:07:14,490 --> 00:07:20,940
That's why we use article a here. And also we use article a with job titles.

97
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:24,990
So that's something you probably will use often, right

98
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:33,280
For example, Jim has worked as a QA analyst for two years now. As a QA analyst.

99
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:41,460
So before job titles, when we name what we do, right, we use article a. I am a QA analyst.

100
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,010
I am a developer.

101
00:07:44,490 --> 00:07:47,340
I am a project manager, like that.

102
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:55,110
And also sometimes we use article a in some set expressions.

103
00:07:55,110 --> 00:08:01,950
So you just have to remember, for example, we have a sprint review meeting once a week.

104
00:08:02,130 --> 00:08:10,650
So when we talk about frequency, when we talk how often something happens, we use article a.

105
00:08:12,570 --> 00:08:16,900
Once a week, twice a week, three times a week.

106
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:18,810
So that's how we say it.

107
00:08:19,260 --> 00:08:20,430
Use article a.

108
00:08:21,150 --> 00:08:28,170
Also, when we talk about speed, the speed limit in urban areas is 50 kilometres an hour.

109
00:08:29,220 --> 00:08:31,560
An hour, right.

110
00:08:32,850 --> 00:08:36,750
Again, when we talk about speed, we use indefinite article a.

111
00:08:38,200 --> 00:08:47,560
And the last one, when we talk about price like this, for example, the basic plan costs $10 a month,

112
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:49,600
$10 a month.

113
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:53,650
And now we will talk about article the.

114
00:08:54,710 --> 00:08:59,810
So the can be used in plural and in singular.

115
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:08,510
So we can use it with one thing, for example, the server and we can use it with many things like the

116
00:09:08,510 --> 00:09:09,530
projects.

117
00:09:10,010 --> 00:09:19,100
We can use it with things we can't count, like that information, well and with many things, as I already

118
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,990
said, the links.

119
00:09:21,770 --> 00:09:25,460
So here we don't have those limits.

120
00:09:25,460 --> 00:09:27,410
Right, we can use it with any word.

121
00:09:27,410 --> 00:09:29,690
Basically, that's how we can put it.

122
00:09:29,690 --> 00:09:31,250
You can use it with any word.

123
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:32,810
All right.

124
00:09:32,810 --> 00:09:39,800
And probably you've noticed that sometimes we say the, usually is the, the, the, but sometimes it's the.

125
00:09:40,250 --> 00:09:44,360
Well again, it has to do with those vowel sounds.

126
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:56,360
Remember a e i o u, like when when we would use an. In those cases, we would also use the, the app.

127
00:09:57,270 --> 00:09:58,640
The engineer.

128
00:09:58,650 --> 00:09:59,430
Right.

129
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,270
But that deadline, the code.

130
00:10:03,420 --> 00:10:13,170
So when we start with vowel, vowel, we would use the, the app, the end, and it's also easier to say

131
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:14,460
this way, right

132
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:16,980
It just goes like that.

133
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:19,470
Easier to say the app than the app.

134
00:10:19,890 --> 00:10:20,880
I think it is easier.

135
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:21,420
Right.

136
00:10:22,370 --> 00:10:24,000
Okay, now let's move on.

137
00:10:29,270 --> 00:10:31,190
When do we use article the?

138
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:33,230
So let's read an example

139
00:10:33,230 --> 00:10:39,140
first. The message I got yesterday says we are going to have a new person on our team.

140
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:44,650
So remember, previous example was I got a message.

141
00:10:45,620 --> 00:10:49,150
Now today I talk about that message again.

142
00:10:49,160 --> 00:10:56,420
This time I say that the message I got yesterday says we are going to have a new person on our team.

143
00:10:56,780 --> 00:11:02,780
Well, it's clear to me and to someone I'm talking to what message I have in mind.

144
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:03,380
Right.

145
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:05,900
This is the message that I got yesterday.

146
00:11:05,900 --> 00:11:11,390
And this is the message that says that we are going to have a new person on our team.

147
00:11:12,560 --> 00:11:13,070
All right.

148
00:11:13,070 --> 00:11:14,060
So use that one.

149
00:11:14,060 --> 00:11:17,060
You already know what you're talking about.

150
00:11:18,110 --> 00:11:22,700
Also, we use article the with superlatives.

151
00:11:22,940 --> 00:11:27,320
In our case, outsourcing is the best option.

152
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,460
The best.

153
00:11:29,180 --> 00:11:31,610
So good, better, the best.

154
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:33,980
The best is a superlative.

155
00:11:34,580 --> 00:11:36,290
In this case, we use the.

156
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:40,820
And also we will cover superlatives later in the course.

157
00:11:40,820 --> 00:11:49,190
So don't worry, the best, the worst, the most interesting in all these cases, we use the.

158
00:11:50,390 --> 00:11:51,410
All right.

159
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:59,660
The last one, if you use your phone number as a password, hackers can easily guess the first two digits.

160
00:12:01,460 --> 00:12:02,120
All right.

161
00:12:02,120 --> 00:12:08,660
So we use the with ordinal numbers. What are ordinal numbers?

162
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:17,540
The first, the second, the third, the forth, the 10th, the 30th and so on.

163
00:12:17,690 --> 00:12:18,350
Right.

164
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:25,610
So like which, not one, but the first.

165
00:12:25,610 --> 00:12:32,240
Right, not two, but the second. In this case we use article the as well.

166
00:12:37,430 --> 00:12:37,730
Okay.

167
00:12:37,730 --> 00:12:38,510
What else?

168
00:12:38,540 --> 00:12:43,790
A few more things to remember when it comes to articles the. We use

169
00:12:43,910 --> 00:12:46,260
We use the in certain expressions.

170
00:12:46,280 --> 00:12:52,700
Look, for example, we always say At the top, for example, at the top of the page.

171
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,410
In the end, in the end of the day. In the middle,

172
00:12:57,680 --> 00:12:59,150
in the middle of the meeting.

173
00:12:59,390 --> 00:13:00,320
On the right.

174
00:13:00,350 --> 00:13:01,310
On the left.

175
00:13:02,090 --> 00:13:07,040
In all those cases, you don't have to think Oh, a or the? It's always the.

176
00:13:07,460 --> 00:13:09,980
It's just a set expression, so you have to remember it.

177
00:13:10,940 --> 00:13:17,960
Then we use the with things that are unique, like they maybe unique in nature,

178
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:21,500
like here the sun, the moon, the world.

179
00:13:21,500 --> 00:13:22,220
Right

180
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,500
Or the Internet.

181
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:25,670
Right.

182
00:13:25,670 --> 00:13:36,800
It's also a unique thing and also used with the article the. The internet. Okay, what else? We use article 

183
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:39,100
the with some proper names.

184
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:47,030
Well you remember I told at the beginning of this lesson we don't use the with geographical names.

185
00:13:47,030 --> 00:13:47,720
Right

186
00:13:47,720 --> 00:13:53,660
For example, we wouldn't say the India, right?

187
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:57,350
No, India, but there are some exceptions.

188
00:13:58,520 --> 00:13:59,870
They USA.

189
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:01,840
The UK.

190
00:14:02,200 --> 00:14:03,730
The Netherlands. 

191
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:04,990
The Alps.

192
00:14:05,290 --> 00:14:06,910
The Indian Ocean.

193
00:14:07,450 --> 00:14:08,440
The Amazon.

194
00:14:09,270 --> 00:14:13,410
So usually when it comes to

195
00:14:15,930 --> 00:14:20,640
countries, we use articles the, when there are words like that - states.

196
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:28,170
So when these words are inside the name of the country states, kingdom, when those geographical names

197
00:14:28,170 --> 00:14:35,010
are in plural, the Netherlands, right, the name of the country is in plural, which as in the end, 

198
00:14:35,030 --> 00:14:36,600
so we use it with the.

199
00:14:36,630 --> 00:14:46,710
The Philippines also, for example. With mountain ranges, the Alps, with the oceans, the Indian Ocean

200
00:14:46,710 --> 00:14:49,380
and with the rivers, the Amazon.

201
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:54,900
So this is not that Amazon company, but the river Amazon.

202
00:14:56,880 --> 00:14:57,750
All right.

203
00:14:57,750 --> 00:15:01,230
And let's move on. Guys,

204
00:15:01,230 --> 00:15:03,120
there are also cases

205
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:05,730
when we have to use no article

206
00:15:05,730 --> 00:15:06,210
Right.

207
00:15:06,390 --> 00:15:09,150
Well, it's important to use no article.

208
00:15:09,240 --> 00:15:14,460
You also need to know what those cases are to sound correct.

209
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:23,250
So, for example, we use no article when we say something plus number, for example, terminal seven.

210
00:15:24,120 --> 00:15:25,050
No article.

211
